T EntrySpecification       | EntryPanel.h | 75-117 | owning                        | -  | Every reading the sections edit, and the presentation the artist left the panel in. `AssetSpecification` are. `14` §4.1 places what the artist chose to look at beside the document and not inside it, so a host threading a pointer in would make closing a workspace a destructive edit. it demonstrates and exercises `ControlPanel`, and a reading of it wired to a brush would make the same control authoritative in two panels at once — which is the divergence `14` §1 forbids. controls sharing one carry are two controls that open together, and two dropdowns doing it is the defect `DropdownCarry`'s own note names.
    has   Coverage          double                       [-]  ?
    has   StrokeExtent      double                       [-]  ?
    has   Hardness          double                       [-]  ?
    has   Displacement      double                       [-]  ?
    has   Turn              double                       [-]  ?
